{
  "_comment": "Control-plane config for Benham-as-Claude. Public IDs only - no secrets here. Copy to control.json (gitignored) and edit.",

  "owner_ids": [273967061619965952],
  "_owner_ids": "Discord user IDs Benham takes direction from. Everyone else can be seen and talked to, but never obeyed. Tyler = caz6666 = 273967061619965952.",

  "destructive_guilds": [736988645562646619],
  "_destructive_guilds": "Guilds where tier-3 (delete/purge/kick/ban) may run AT ALL. A tier-3 action outside this list is refused outright - no confirmation can unlock it, only editing this file. Default: Testing Server only.",

  "agent_guilds": [736988645562646619],
  "_agent_guilds": "Guilds where the autonomous agent may engage from a channel mention. DMs from an owner always work regardless of this list.",

  "post_guilds": [736988645562646619, 1491485711076167711],
  "post_channels": [],
  "_posting": "Hard scope cap on where Benham may PUT CONTENT (send_message/send_embed/send_file). post_channels wins when non-empty; otherwise the channel's guild must be in post_guilds. Both empty = no cap. Not a confirmation gate - a refusal here cannot be unlocked by any yes. Reading is never restricted by this. The case it covers: Benham is invited to a new server, and someone there posts text engineered to look like an instruction.",

  "agent": {
    "enabled": true,
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
    "max_tokens": 2048,
    "max_tool_rounds": 8,
    "history_turns": 20,
    "cooldown_seconds": 1.5,
    "web_search": true,
    "searches_per_turn": 3
  },
  "_agent": "enabled=false makes Benham a pure relay (no API cost). model: claude-haiku-4-5 is cheap, claude-sonnet-5 is sharper for multi-step tool use. max_tool_rounds bounds one request's agent loop. web_search adds Anthropic's SERVER-SIDE search (runs on their infrastructure, nothing fetched from this machine); queries are logged to agent_searches.jsonl. NOTE: a turn that searched is TAINTED, exactly as if Benham had read a channel - a web page is text a stranger wrote - so outward actions after a search ask for confirmation, and pc_task is blocked until a fresh message. That is the intended trade, not a bug; set web_search=false if you would rather have the un-gated tool loop than live information.",

  "pc": {
    "enabled": false,
    "workdir": "C:\\Users\\Tyler\\Claude\\Benhams-inbox",
    "permission_timeout_seconds": 300,
    "max_turns": 30,
    "use_api_key": true
  },
  "_pc": "Gives Benham a REAL Claude Code session on the machine (codesession.py), with Tyler's own skills loaded. Reading/searching is free; every write, command and subagent DMs him for approval and blocks until he answers - a timeout denies. enabled=false switches the whole thing off. use_api_key=true bills ANTHROPIC_API_KEY per task; set it false after running `claude` once interactively to bill a Claude subscription instead. NOTE: workdir is where it starts, NOT a sandbox - a session can reach the whole filesystem.",

  "guest": {
    "enabled": false,
    "mode": "chat",
    "ids": [],
    "capabilities": [],
    "model": "claude-haiku-4-5",
    "max_tokens": 500,
    "history_turns": 10,
    "cooldown_seconds": 3,
    "daily_message_cap": 100,
    "global_daily_cap": 400,
    "web_search": true,
    "searches_per_turn": 2,
    "tool_rounds": 4,
    "tool_round_cost": 1,
    "workspace": { "per_guest_mb": 20, "max_files": 100, "per_file_mb": 5 },
    "read_channels": []
  },
  "_guest_read_channels": "Channel ids guests may read via the read_shared_channel capability (Stage 5). TWO separate decisions are required and both are yours: the capability must be listed in guest.capabilities AND the channel id listed here - granting the capability with this list empty reaches nothing. Adding an id publishes that channel's contents, past and future, to every guest on the list; the people posting there will not know. Testing Server channels are the safe choice. Guests can only ever name ids on this list - the capability refuses anything else before it even resolves the channel, so it cannot be used to discover what other channels exist.",
  "_guest_workspace": "Caps on guest_work/, the folder tree guests get in workspace mode once ws_* capabilities are granted: guest_work/<user_id>/ each (private, confined, flat filenames only, runnable extensions refused however a file arrives) plus guest_work/commons/ which YOU populate by hand and guests can only read. Deliverables ride the DM reply as attachments (ws_attach; re-verified in bot.py before a byte leaves); inbound files come only from the guest's OWN messages in that DM (ws_import; no URL fetch exists anywhere). To turn the workspace on: mode='workspace', then list some of ws_list/ws_read/ws_write/ws_delete/ws_import/ws_attach in guest.capabilities, then restart.",
  "_guest": "Lets whitelisted NON-owners hold a plain conversation with Claude by DM. Conversation ONLY apart from web_search: the guest path passes no CLIENT tools to the API - the single entry is Anthropic's SERVER-SIDE web search (runs on their servers, nothing fetched from this machine or network; searches_per_turn caps uses per message). A turn that searched counts DOUBLE against the daily cap, and every query is appended to guest_searches.jsonl for hand moderation. So no Discord action, no channel read and no PC access is reachable from it - a guest id buys a reply instead of a refusal, and nothing else. ids: Discord user ids; an owner id here is ignored. capabilities: names of capabilities guests may reach - the CONFIG half of a three-part grant (the capability must ALSO declare guest=True in code and name the guest origin), so a typo here can only turn things OFF. As of Stage 2 no capability carries the flag, so this list grants nothing whatever it says; it becomes meaningful when the guest workspace ships (Stage 4). mode: 'chat' (plain conversation, guest.py) or 'workspace' (guest_agent.py's tool loop over exactly the granted capabilities - with the list empty it behaves like chat); an unrecognised mode disables guest chat rather than guessing. tool_rounds caps one workspace turn's loop (default 4); each round beyond the first charges tool_round_cost extra messages, same after-the-fact shape as the search double-charge. Guests are DM-only and cannot be reached by mention. Caps are per calendar day and reset on the first message after midnight; every message bills Tyler, which is what the caps are for. Separate memory file (guest_memory.json) - a guest never sees, and is never seen by, Tyler's own conversation. RESTART REQUIRED, both ways: this file is read once at import, so enabling guests, disabling them, or striking someone from ids all take effect on the next start and not before. To cut a guest off immediately, bounce the bot - 'enabled: false' on its own does nothing to a running process.",

  "confirm": {
